+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The service already ships coupon storage (`coupons`, `coupon_redemptions`) and a
+coupon admin API, but an order can never be discounted: there is no way to apply
+a coupon to an order. `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` is required so customers
+can redeem fixed-amount and percentage coupons against their orders.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add endpoint `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` with request body
+  `{ "couponCode": "SAVE20" }`.
+- Validate coupon eligibility before applying: the coupon must exist, be
+  `ACTIVE`, be within its validity window (relative to the injected clock), the
+  order amount must meet the coupon minimum, and the coupon usage limit must not
+  be exhausted.
+- Compute the discount for both coupon types: `FIXED` (integer cents) and
+  `PERCENT` (0..100), honouring `max_discount_cents` and never discounting more
+  than the order amount.
+- Persist `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents` and `coupon_code` on the order,
+  record a `coupon_redemptions` row and increment the coupon `used_count`
+  atomically.
+- Return the updated order (same shape as other order endpoints).
+- Only `PENDING` orders can be discounted; an order that already carries a
+  coupon cannot be discounted again.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupons`: applying a coupon to an order - eligibility rules, discount
+  computation for fixed and percentage coupons, and the resulting order state.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None: no existing spec-level behavior changes. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts` - new route.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts` - `applyCoupon` business rules.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` / `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts` -
+  persistence of the discount, redemption and usage counter.
+- `src/app.ts` - wire the coupon repository into `OrderService`.
+- `src/db.ts` - no schema change; existing tables are used.
+- API: new endpoint; existing endpoints unchanged.
