+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyDiscount(id, { discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode })` to write `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents` and `coupon_code`; verify with a repository-level check or the order body returned by the endpoint.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)` covering the `coupon_redemptions` insert and the `used_count` increment; verify a redemption row and incremented `usedCount` are observable after a successful apply.
+- [x] 1.3 Wrap the order update plus redemption/usage writes in a single transaction helper (`withTransaction`) so a failure rolls back all three; verify a forced failure leaves `used_count` and the order unchanged.
+
+## 2. Service and HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` performing the ordered eligibility checks (order exists → `PENDING` → no existing coupon → coupon exists → usable by status and clock → minimum amount → usage limit) and throwing the `AppError` codes from the spec; verify each rejection with a test.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement the discount math (`FIXED` value, `PERCENT` `Math.floor(amount * value / 100)`, `max_discount_cents` cap, clamp to order amount) and persist via the transaction; verify the fixed, percentage, cap and clamp scenarios from the spec.
+- [x] 2.3 Wire `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts` and register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`; verify the route returns 200 with the updated order for a valid request.
+
+## 3. Tests
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering the happy paths (fixed and percentage) and the error codes `INVALID_REQUEST`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `ORDER_ALREADY_HAS_COUPON`, `COUPON_NOT_ACTIVE`, `COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT_NOT_MET`, `COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED`; verify with `npm test`.
+- [x] 3.2 Verify redemption accounting in the test file: `usedCount` increases by one and a `coupon_redemptions` row exists after success, and neither happens after a failed apply.
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` (type check) and `npm test` (full suite) and confirm both pass; verify the pre-existing `tests/orders.test.ts` behavior is unaffected.
